  "scientific_notes": [
    "The sole fitted scalar is the convex interpolation from global angle damping to the PSD local damping factorization. The original T0M1 stiffness, D0, memory ports and rates remain fixed; rho=2/3 and scale1 are fixed in the weak force kernel.",
    "One shared symmetric PSD damping root serves the complete train cohort. Each genuine observed path is truncated at most to311 frames, has its own interval normalization and memory projection, and contributes once to the complete-train cross and curvature statistics.",
    "The exact one-dimensional optimum is clipped to[0,1], with raw optimum, curvature, gradient and boundary retained. Finite full-cohort data, rank10 and quadrature gap<=1e-10 establish fit support; the separate scientific gate requires lower spatial SSE than global SSE in train, stable and unstable groups.",
    "The fixed trace-matched isotropic control is reported without fitting, preserving visibility into average-damping versus spatial effects. No test statistic determines the coefficient or gate.",
    "Only a numerically supported strictly positive coefficient defines a distinct spatial forecast candidate. A zero coefficient reproduces the existing global law; any complete frozen evaluation requires its own registration. Free memory elimination is a fitting nuisance and is not supplied as a causal forecast initializer."
